        <main class="col-12 col-lg" id="main" tabindex="-1">
            <article aria-label="IN.gov Content">
            
                                                            





              

            
    <div class="light" id="subpage-banner-container" style="background-image: url('/dA/1e0dc29a09/banner-news.jpg?force_download=1&filename=banner-news.jpg'); background-position: center center;">
        <div id="subpage-banner-overlay">
            <div id="subpage-banner-width">
            
                                                    <h1 id="subpage-main-title">Judicial Retention</h1>
                
                                                    <ul id="subpage-breadcrumbs">
                                                    <li style="display:inline">
                                                                    <span class="fa-light fa-home"></span>
                                                                                                     <a href="/courts/index">Courts</a>
                                                            </li>
                                                                                                <li style="display:inline">
                            <span class="fa-light fa-angle-right"></span>
                            <span>Judicial Retention</span>
                        </li>
                                            </ul>
                            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
                                    
                
                                    
                                                                                                                                                
                                                                                                    
                    <section class="">
                        <div class="row">

                                                                              
                                                                                                        
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-lg-12  ">
                                                                <div class="generic-content-wrap h-100"
    >
    <blockquote>"The health of our entire legal system&mdash;both state and federal&mdash;depends on having a competent and independent state judiciary... How we choose our state judges, and how we decide whether to keep them in office or not, is of critical importance."</blockquote>
<p style="text-align: right;">&mdash;the Honorable Sandra Day O'Connor<br /><em>Retired Associate Justice, Supreme Court of the United States</em></p>
<h2>Judges up for Retention</h2>
<p>The next judicial retention election for state appellate judges will take place in November 2026.</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="#deboer">Hon. Mary DeBoer</a>, Court of Appeals</li>
<li><a href="#felix">Hon. Paul Felix</a>, Court of Appeals</li>
<li><a href="#kenworthy">Hon. Dana Kenworthy</a>, Court of Appeals</li>
<li><a href="#mcadam">Hon. Justin McAdam</a>, Tax Court</li>
</ul>
</div>
                            </div>
                            
                                                  </div>
                    </section>
                    
                                                                                                                                                
                                                                                                    
                    <section class="">
                        <div class="row">

                                                                              
                                                                                                        
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-lg-12  ">
                                                                <div class="generic-content-wrap h-100"
    >
    <h2>About Judicial Retention</h2>
<p><a href="/courts/about/retention">Learn more about Indiana's judicial retention system</a></p>
<p>State Bar Association Survey Results:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://www.inbar.org/news/736160/-Bar-members-say-yes-to-judges-up-for-retention-next-month.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bar members say &lsquo;yes&rsquo; to judges up for retention next month</a></li>
</ul>
<p>Statutes regarding retention of Appellate Judges:</p>
<ul>
<li>Supreme Court Justices, see <a href="http://www.in.gov/legislative/ic/code/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Indiana Code</a> 33-24-2</li>
<li>Court of Appeals Judges, see&nbsp;<a href="http://www.in.gov/legislative/ic/code/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Indiana Code</a> 33-25-2</li>
<li>Tax Court Judges, see&nbsp;<a href="http://www.in.gov/legislative/ic/code/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Indiana Code</a> 33-26-2</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<p><em>This information is prepared by the Indiana Office of Judicial Administration (IOJA). IOJA does not endorse the results of any surveys on judicial retention or the views expressed on any website outside the Indiana Judicial Branch website.</em></p>
</div>
                            </div>
                            
                                                  </div>
                    </section>
                    
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                                                                                                
                    <section class="">
                        <div class="row">

                                                                              
                                                                                                        
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-lg-9  ">
                                                                <div class="generic-content-wrap h-100"
    >
    <h2><strong><a id="deboer"></a>Judge Mary A. DeBoer</strong></h2>
<p><strong>Mary A. DeBoer</strong>&nbsp;grew up in Kalamazoo, Michigan and relocated permanently to Valparaiso, Indiana in 1990. She graduated with honors from Western Michigan University in 1989 and earned her J.D. from Valparaiso University School of Law in 1993. Judge DeBoer served as a deputy prosecutor and as a magistrate for Starke and Porter Counties. She was appointed as the Porter Circuit Court Judge in 2019 by Governor Eric J. Holcomb, who later appointed her to serve on the Court of Appeals of Indiana in 2024.</p>
<p>Judge DeBoer has worked in public service and private practice. As a private attorney, her focus was primarily on family law, personal injury, and medical malpractice cases. Her thirteen-year career as a deputy prosecutor reinforced her desire to protect vulnerable... [<a href="/courts/appeals/judges/mary-deboer">Read more</a>]</p>
<p><a href="/courts/appeals/judges/mary-deboer"><span class="fa fas fa-user"> </span>Biography</a></p>
<p><a href="https://mycourts.in.gov/arguments/default.aspx?judge=251" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span class="fa fas fa-video"> </span>Oral argument videos</a></p>
<p><a href="https://public.courts.in.gov/decisions?j=109631" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span class="fa fas fa-book"> </span>Opinions</a></p>
</div>
                            </div>
                            
                                                                              
                                                                                                        
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-lg-3  ">
                                                                <div class="generic-content-wrap h-100"
    >
    <p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/dA/bb4ca9e7c7/deboer.jpg?language_id=1" alt="Judge Mary DeBoer portrait" data-field-name="fileAsset" data-inode="914bf994-3412-43d4-a802-de8b54c7dd2f" data-identifier="bb4ca9e7c72987ade0dcbf2ef50a4932" data-saveas="deboer.jpg" width="300" height="420" /><br />Hon. Mary DeBoer</p>
</div>
                            </div>
                            
                                                  </div>
                    </section>
                    
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                                                                                                
                    <section class="">
                        <div class="row">

                                                                              
                                                                                                        
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-lg-9  ">
                                                                <div class="generic-content-wrap h-100"
    >
    <h2><a id="felix"></a>Hon. Paul A Felix</h2>
<p>Paul A. Felix was appointed to the Court of Appeals by Governor Holcomb and began his service on July 28, 2023.</p>
<p>Judge Felix was born in Elkhart. He was raised in Greenwood and attended Whiteland schools. He earned his undergraduate and law degrees from Indiana University - Bloomington.</p>
<p>Following graduation, Judge Felix served as a Deputy Prosecuting Attorney in the Johnson County Prosecutor&rsquo;s Office from 1995 to 2006. During his prosecuting career, he created the county&rsquo;s first Domestic Violence Unit and led the prosecution of DV cases for three years.&nbsp;</p>
<p>In 2007, Judge Felix was appointed to the Carmel City Court by Governor Mitch Daniels. In 2009, he was elected to serve as the Hamilton Circuit Court Judge, where he served for 14 years. In... [<a href="/courts/appeals/judges/paul-felix">Read more</a>]</p>
<p><a href="/courts/appeals/judges/paul-felix"><span class="fa fas fa-user"> </span>Biography</a></p>
<p><a href="https://mycourts.in.gov/arguments/default.aspx?judge=248" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span class="fa fas fa-video"> </span>Oral argument videos</a></p>
<p><a href="https://public.courts.in.gov/decisions?j=106858" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span class="fa fas fa-book"> </span>Opinions</a></p>
</div>
