    <h2><a id="mcadam"></a>Hon. Justin L. McAdam</h2>
<p>Justin L. McAdam is the third judge to serve on the Indiana Tax Court since its creation in 1986, following Judge Thomas G. Fisher and Judge Martha Blood Wentworth. He was appointed by Governor Eric J. Holcomb and took the bench on September 1, 2023.</p>
<p>Judge McAdam was born in San Diego, California, and lived in Florida and Colorado before his family eventually settled in Terre Haute, Indiana, in 1992. After graduating from Terre Haute North Vigo High School, he began his college career studying mathematics at Purdue University. He later transferred to Indiana University, where he earned Bachelor of Arts degrees in economics and political science in 2005, graduating Phi Beta Kappa with highest distinction.</p>
<p>After college, Judge McAdam was awarded a Governor&rsquo;s Fellowship... [<a href="/courts/tax/justin-mcadam">Read more</a>]</p>
<p><a href="/courts/tax/justin-mcadam"><span class="fa fas fa-user"> </span>Biography</a></p>
